 "body_html": "<p>See this demo:</p>\n<pre class=\"lang-cpp prettyprint-override\"><code>#include &lt;malloc.h&gt;\n#include &lt;stdio.h&gt;\n#include &lt;stdlib.h&gt;\n\nvoid Pause() {\n    int v; {\n        scanf(&quot;%d&quot;, &amp;v);\n    }\n}\n\nint main(int argc, char **argv) {\n    Pause();\n    printf(&quot;Hello.\\n&quot;);\n    malloc_trim(0);\n    Pause();\n    return 0;\n}\n</code></pre>\n<p>mem status at the first <code>pause()</code>:</p>\n<pre><code>root     1288815  0.0  0.0  15616   844 pts/1    S+   21:13   0:00 ./a.out\n</code></pre>\n<p>mem status at the second <code>pause()</code>:</p>\n<pre><code>root     1288815  0.0  0.0  15620   844 pts/1    S+   21:13   0:00 ./a.out\n</code></pre>\n<p>I used <code>malloc_trim(0)</code> to make sure the released memory has been returned to OS, then I used pmap and found that the program allocated a page of memory on heap and won't be released. What is it?<br />\nI'm using centos.</p>\n",
